<title>AUSTRALIA: Gutnick criticises Australia gold analysts.</title>
<headline>Gutnick criticises Australia gold analysts.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mining entrepreneur Joseph Gutnick criticised Australian gold analysts and brokers on Wednesday, saying their persistent negativity was holding back investment in Australian gold companies and in gold exploration.</p>
<p>Gutnick said in a luncheon speech to the Australia-Israel Chamber of Commerce that local analysts were much more critical of Australian gold groups than U.S. analysts.</p>
<p>He also said many of Australia's largest resource companies, including Rio Tinto Ltd, would eventually be embarassed about their decisions to scale back Australian exploration as smaller local groups like his stepped profitably into the gap.</p>
</text>
